# tuned/repo.env -- llama.cpp-specific settings for tuned builds. Sourced by
# tuned/env.sh after the shared device and toolkit definitions (tuned/common-data,
# from zbrad/tuned-common). Tracked, so a release is reproducible.
#
# This file may only ADD repo-specific settings. Changing any shared key
# (GPU_TUNED_*, CUDA_*, TOOLKIT_*) is a loud error from env.sh.
#
# Plain assignment on purpose: this file is sourced inside a function, where
# `declare` would make the variable local and lose it.

# CMake options for the release build. Read from the configured build/
# (CMakeCache.txt) and the build command in .claude/settings.local.json, 2026-10-09.
# The arch and compiler come from the shared files (release.sh adds them).
# GGML_CUDA_NCCL=ON links NCCL. Where it comes from is decided per toolkit (tuned/env.sh): a zbrad/nccl release
# pinned in tuned/nccl.pins, linked statically, or the system libnccl2 pinned by the toolkit's TOOLKIT_NCCL_VERSION
# and bundled by package.sh. Either way it must have been built for that toolkit's CUDA.
LLAMA_TUNED_CMAKE_FLAGS=(
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    -DGGML_CUDA=ON
    -DGGML_CUDA_FA=ON
    -DGGML_CUDA_GRAPHS=ON
    -DGGML_CUDA_NCCL=ON
    -DGGML_CUDA_COMPRESSION_MODE=size
    -DLLAMA_OPENSSL=ON
)
# LLAMA_OPENSSL=ON is required, not incidental: without it every HTTPS use fails
# at runtime ("HTTPS is not supported", common/http.h) -- model downloads from
# Hugging Face or by URL (router mode, open-webui Model Services) and serving
# over TLS (--ssl-key-file). It is the upstream default; it is listed here so a
# change of that default cannot silently drop TLS. It links libssl.so.3 and
# libcrypto.so.3 (apt libssl3t64).
